    "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements **ADR-026: CSS Variable Resolution** (`:root` selector + `var()` pre-resolution). Three commits.\n\n**Honest framing:** this PR's visible win is a **bug fix** (CSS text no longer renders as article content). The var() resolution infrastructure ships correctly and is tested, but produces **negligible visible delta** over ADR-025 on Wikipedia. It's the mechanism ADR-027 (`@media`) and ADR-028 (`:not()` + attribute operators) will use when their rules finally reach the cascade.\n\n## What shipped\n\n### Primary visible win: display:none inline-flattening fix\n\nWikipedia ships 18 `<style>` tags in `<body>` (TemplateStyles extension), several nested inside inline elements. Before this PR, their CSS text (e.g. `.navbar-ct-mini{font-size:114%;margin:0 4em}`) was rendering as **visible article content**.\n\n**Root cause**: cascade correctly computed `display: none` for all 18 (verified by diagnostic — both head- and body-position `<style>` report `display=[none]`). But `flatten_inline_to_words` recursed into `display:none` descendants without checking, so any style tag inside an inline element had its text content flattened into the article body.\n\n**Pre-existing bug** — never triggered by synthetic tests because they don't nest `<style>` inside inline elements. Surfaced by ADR-026's required visual verification.\n\n**Fix**: one-line check at the top of `flatten_inline_to_words`'s Element branch. Regression test covers `<p><span>before <style>...</style> after</span></p>`: asserts CSS text absent from layout, \"before\"/\"after\" text preserved.\n\n### Infrastructure: var() resolution\n\nWhole-value `var(--x[, fallback])` declarations resolve at `Stylesheet::parse()` time against a per-sheet variable map extracted from `:root` rules.\n\n- **`SimpleKind::PseudoRoot`**: parser + matcher (`true` iff element has no parent element) + specificity (class weight, CSS 2.1 semantics).\n- **`Stylesheet::variables`**: `unordered_map<string, string>`, populated from canonical `:root`-only rules.\n- **`resolve_var_whole`**: parses `var(--x, Y)`; three outcomes (`NotVar` / `Resolved` / `Failed`). Failed → declaration dropped per CSS computed-value-time semantics.\n- **Post-parse pass**: walks all rules, resolves var() in non-custom-property declarations.\n- **Single-pass only**: recursive variables deferred (1 case on Wikipedia; consumers fall back anyway).\n\n## The measurement that mattered (and the honest delta)\n\n**Context measurement** (from ADR-026 spec): 542 `var()` declarations on Wikipedia. 341 whole-value; 299 of those target properties our layout engine reads (**84.2%**). 194 partial-value (left unchanged — targets consumed properties only 20% of the time). 7 multi-var.\n\n**Post-implementation visual measurement**: **negligible visible delta over ADR-025.** Screenshots before/after are visually indistinguishable. The 299 resolutions are real (verified by unit tests + cascade integration), but they don't produce perceptible change on Wikipedia.\n\n**Root cause hypothesis** (would need one more diagnostic to confirm which dominates):\n1. **Cascade loss** — rules containing var() may lose specificity against higher-priority rules. E.g. `--color-base: #202122` resolves on 27 declarations, but blue link rules may still win on sidebar `<a>` tags (visible: sidebar links are still blue, not dark gray).\n2. **Media-gating** — some rules with var() declarations are inside `@media` blocks (not parsed yet — ADR-027), so the var() never reaches the cascade.\n3. **Visual similarity** — resolved values may be nearly identical to what ADR-025 already applies.\n\n## Meta-lesson-v3 (documented in the ADR)\n\n**Consumed-property coverage is necessary, not sufficient, for visible change.**\n\nThe rule containing the resolved declaration must **also win the cascade** after parsing:\n- Specificity beats competitors\n- Media-query gating passes\n- Selector parses (pseudo-classes, `:not()`, attribute operators)\n\nSame shape as ADR-023's \"2,500 `<a>` per wrapper not 10\" and ADR-024's \"measured prediction needs a code-path model\" — a metric that looks like the answer but isn't.\n\n**Refined rule**: when claiming a resolution-count implies a visible delta, trace the full cascade path for a sample of declarations. **Consumed-property coverage + cascade-winner status + visible-difference are three separate properties, not one.**\n\n## Why ADR-026 still matters\n\nThe var() resolver is the mechanism ADR-027 (`@media`) and ADR-028 (`:not()` + attribute operators) will use once their rules reach the cascade. When `@media` blocks parse, their rules finally reach the cascade; when they win, their declarations already have concrete values instead of dead `var()` references. ADR-026 ships the infrastructure that makes those ADRs possible.\n\nSame pattern as **ADR-022 → ADR-023**: ADR-022 shipped targeted cascade (no visible change for wrapper hovers, real infrastructure); ADR-023 used it to deliver the visible win. ADR-026 ships var() resolution (no visible change today); ADR-027 uses it to unlock layout rules that will produce visible change.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Commit | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| `d979198` | `:root` selector + `Stylesheet::variables`. 8 tests. |\n| `7fd29e2` | `var()` resolution pass + display:none inline fix. 9 var() tests + 1 regression test. |\n| `8824de2` | Docs: ADR-026 status → Implemented, README, CHANGELOG, Meta-lesson-v3. |\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-026: 288 cases, 1239 assertions\n- After Commit 1: 296 cases, 1266 assertions (+8)\n- After Commit 2: 306 cases, 1297 assertions (+10: 9 var() + 1 regression)\n- Zero warnings, zero failures\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| CSS text no longer renders as article content | ✅ (screenshot before/after) |\n| Article body prose starts cleanly | ✅ |\n| var() resolution to defined var | ✅ (unit test) |\n| var() undefined + fallback | ✅ |\n| var() undefined + no fallback → drop | ✅ |\n| Partial-value var() left unchanged | ✅ |\n| Custom-property declarations not resolved | ✅ |\n| Fallback with nested parens (`rgb()`) | ✅ |\n| Malformed var() dropped | ✅ |\n| `:root` matches `<html>` not `<body>` | ✅ |\n| Visible delta over ADR-025 | ⚠️ **negligible** (honest, documented) |\n\n## Not included (deferred)\n\n- Partial-value substitution + `calc()` evaluation\n- Recursive `var()` (1 case on Wikipedia)\n- Element-scoped custom properties (`.theme-dark { --bg: black }`)\n- Dynamic variable cascade (`:hover`-changing variables)\n- Keyword fallbacks (`inherit`/`initial`/`unset`, 17 cases)\n- Merged UA+author variable maps\n- `env()` environment variables\n\n## The four-ADR arc\n\n| ADR | Status | Visible delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| **025** | merged | Article content styled (~40-50% improvement) |\n| **026** | this PR | Bug fix visible; var() infra ships; **no visible delta from var() alone** |\n| **027** | next (`@media`) | Expected visible: layout rules unlock sidebar/header/TOC; var() resolutions there become visible |\n| **028** | after (`:not()` + attr-ops) | Expected visible: remaining structural rules |\n\nADR-027 is the natural next step: it's where the var() infrastructure finally produces visible delta, and it's where the layout rules ADR-025 missed become reachable.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/026-css-variables.md` — status now **Implemented**, with Implementation section documenting the measured coverage, honest negligible-delta, Meta-lesson-v3, and the display:none fix.\n\nRefs #155\n",
